WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.266 --> 00:00:01.901 line:92%
-So, this show "A.P. Bio" --

00:00:01.901 --> 00:00:03.670 align:start size:94% position:6%
full disclosure,
because I love this show,

00:00:03.670 --> 00:00:06.573 align:start size:94% position:6%
but I am one of the producers
on this show, and --

00:00:06.573 --> 00:00:08.742 size:84% position:42% line:92%
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:00:08.742 --> 00:00:11.444 align:start size:94% position:6%
I'm so happy that you are
playing this role.

00:00:11.444 --> 00:00:12.846 line:92%
You are playing a teacher who --

00:00:12.846 --> 00:00:15.048 align:start size:94% position:6%
we sort of set it up
in the clip --

00:00:15.048 --> 00:00:16.249 line:92%
but you are not a good person.

00:00:16.249 --> 00:00:18.485 align:start size:94% position:6%
Would you say that's accurate
on the show?

00:00:18.485 --> 00:00:21.154 size:81% position:41%
-Yeah. I'd say that's
pretty accurate, yeah,

00:00:21.154 --> 00:00:23.556
or at least I'm trying not to be
a good person.

00:00:23.556 --> 00:00:26.726 align:start size:94% position:6%
I think the secret sauce
to the show is that

00:00:26.726 --> 00:00:29.396 align:start size:94% position:6%
he is extremely selfish
and narcissistic,

00:00:29.396 --> 00:00:33.233
but ultimately, and I think
the creator, Mike O'Brien --

00:00:33.233 --> 00:00:33.967 line:92%
-Yes, a fantastic writer.

00:00:33.967 --> 00:00:37.237 align:start size:94% position:6%
-He's amazing. He was on "SNL"
for six years as a writer.

00:00:37.237 --> 00:00:40.774 align:start size:94% position:6%
And he's created a character
who puts on this front

00:00:40.774 --> 00:00:42.475 align:start size:94% position:6%
of being extremely selfish
and narcissistic,

00:00:42.475 --> 00:00:44.477
but I think under it all
there is some heart there,

00:00:44.477 --> 00:00:46.780 align:start size:94% position:6%
but yeah, he basically
goes into classes and says,

00:00:46.780 --> 00:00:48.548 align:start size:94% position:6%
"I'm not going to
teach you anything.

00:00:48.548 --> 00:00:49.516 line:92%
This is a free period for you,

00:00:49.516 --> 00:00:53.119 align:start size:94% position:6%
and if you do
what I tell you to do

00:00:53.119 --> 00:00:55.722 align:start size:94% position:6%
and don't try to make me
teach you biology,

00:00:55.722 --> 00:00:58.124 align:start size:94% position:6%
then I'm going to
give you all an A."

00:00:58.124 --> 00:00:58.792 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
Which I think is --

00:00:58.792 --> 00:01:02.195 align:start size:94% position:6%
To most classes that would be
like a sweet deal,

00:01:02.195 --> 00:01:02.762 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
but these kids --

00:01:02.762 --> 00:01:04.397 align:start size:94% position:6%
and this is part of what makes
the show so different --

00:01:04.397 --> 00:01:06.599 size:88% position:44%
is these kids actually
want to learn something,

00:01:06.599 --> 00:01:07.700 line:92%
and that's a problem for me.

00:01:07.700 --> 00:01:08.868 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Yeah.
[ Laughter ]

00:01:08.868 --> 00:01:10.570 align:start size:94% position:6%
-I don't want to
have to do work.

00:01:10.570 --> 00:01:12.338 align:start size:94% position:6%
-You offer them
Advil or Tylenol PM.

00:01:12.338 --> 00:01:15.241
You actually give them a chance
to just take a pill

00:01:15.241 --> 00:01:17.343 align:start size:94% position:6%
and fall asleep for an hour.
[ Laughter ]

00:01:17.343 --> 00:01:19.612 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Yeah, it's basically what you
would want your teachers

00:01:19.612 --> 00:01:21.848 align:start size:94% position:6%
to do when you were in school,
but not these kids.

00:01:21.848 --> 00:01:25.318
-Did you have important teachers
in your life?

00:01:25.318 --> 00:01:28.354 align:start size:94% position:6%
Were you someone who --
-Uh, hmm.

00:01:28.354 --> 00:01:29.823 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
[ Laughter ]

00:01:29.823 --> 00:01:30.490 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
Important teachers?

00:01:30.490 --> 00:01:32.092 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Yeah, that sent you
on your path?

00:01:32.092 --> 00:01:34.694 size:75% position:38%
I mean, you ended up
going to Juilliard.

00:01:34.694 --> 00:01:35.161 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
-I did.

00:01:35.161 --> 00:01:36.663
-So obviously something happened
in high school

00:01:36.663 --> 00:01:40.100 align:start size:94% position:6%
that made you think,
"Oh, I should be an actor.

00:01:40.100 --> 00:01:41.101 size:88% position:44% line:92%
-Yeah, I wouldn't say --

00:01:41.101 --> 00:01:44.337
I didn't have any, like,
"lean on me" type teachers.

00:01:44.337 --> 00:01:45.004 size:75% position:38% line:92%
Any "stand by me's."

00:01:45.004 --> 00:01:47.807
-You didn't have a "lean on me"
or a "stand by me"?

00:01:47.807 --> 00:01:49.442 align:start size:94% position:6%
[ Laughter ]
-Stand by me?

00:01:49.442 --> 00:01:50.310 line:92%
I had no one by me, basically.

00:01:50.310 --> 00:01:53.980
I didn't have any teachers
who like, turned my life around

00:01:53.980 --> 00:01:55.048 size:81% position:41% line:92%
or anything like that.

00:01:55.048 --> 00:01:56.282 line:92%
But, no I tell you, there --

00:01:56.282 --> 00:01:58.885 align:start size:94% position:6%
There was this one teacher
that I loved,

00:01:58.885 --> 00:02:01.321 line:92%
and he was my health teacher.

00:02:01.321 --> 00:02:02.889 line:92%
I think his name was Coach Scott

00:02:02.889 --> 00:02:04.991 align:start size:94% position:6%
'cause he was also
the football coach.

00:02:04.991 --> 00:02:05.558 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
-Uh-huh, yeah.

00:02:05.558 --> 00:02:07.460 align:start size:94% position:6%
-The health teacher is never
just the health teacher.

00:02:07.460 --> 00:02:08.261 line:92%
He's always something else.

00:02:08.261 --> 00:02:10.230
-I think my health teacher was
also our football coach, yeah.

00:02:10.230 --> 00:02:12.732
-Yeah, yeah, I don't know.
Yeah, I don't get that, really.

00:02:12.732 --> 00:02:14.634 align:start size:94% position:6%
I think he was, like,
the offensive line coach

00:02:14.634 --> 00:02:15.435 line:92%
but also the health teacher,

00:02:15.435 --> 00:02:18.905
because I mean, who better to
teach you about, you know,

00:02:18.905 --> 00:02:19.906 line:92%
your budding human sexuality

00:02:19.906 --> 00:02:23.576
than an obese high school
Alabama football coach.

00:02:23.576 --> 00:02:24.144 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
[ Laughter ]

00:02:24.144 --> 00:02:26.613 align:start size:94% position:6%
He's the one you want teaching
you about your body

00:02:26.613 --> 00:02:28.615 align:start size:94% position:6%
and all the feelings
you're feeling.

00:02:28.615 --> 00:02:29.916 line:92%
-I feel like back in the day

00:02:29.916 --> 00:02:31.985 align:start size:94% position:6%
health teacher
was a different thing.

00:02:31.985 --> 00:02:34.888 align:start size:94% position:6%
It was like,
"Who knows how to do squats?"

00:02:34.888 --> 00:02:36.823 align:start size:94% position:6%
But then it became more about
like sex ed,

00:02:36.823 --> 00:02:38.591 align:start size:94% position:6%
and it took a while
for people to adjust

00:02:38.591 --> 00:02:40.693 align:start size:94% position:6%
as to who should be
the better teacher there.

00:02:40.693 --> 00:02:42.495 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Yeah, and it seems like
that's based on

00:02:42.495 --> 00:02:43.830 align:start size:94% position:6%
where you are in the country,
right?

00:02:43.830 --> 00:02:46.466 align:start size:94% position:6%
Because in Alabama, it's like,
we have to talk about sex,

00:02:46.466 --> 00:02:48.468 align:start size:94% position:6%
but we really don't want to
talk about sex,

00:02:48.468 --> 00:02:50.904 align:start size:94% position:6%
but we should,
but we can't, and we will.

00:02:50.904 --> 00:02:52.906 align:start size:94% position:6%
So listening to this man
try to explain

00:02:52.906 --> 00:02:55.775 align:start size:94% position:6%
the secondary sex
characteristics of a female

00:02:55.775 --> 00:02:56.543 size:84% position:42% line:92%
was very uncomfortable.

00:02:56.543 --> 00:02:59.245 align:start size:94% position:6%
-But you had
a very interesting upbringing.

00:02:59.245 --> 00:03:00.580 line:92%
Your dad was in the Air Force,

00:03:00.580 --> 00:03:02.582 align:start size:94% position:6%
so you traveled
all around the world.

00:03:02.582 --> 00:03:03.016 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
-Yeah.

00:03:03.016 --> 00:03:05.351 align:start size:94% position:6%
-And then ended up
in high school in Alabama.

00:03:05.351 --> 00:03:08.555
What was -- By the time you got
to high school, like,

00:03:08.555 --> 00:03:09.889 align:start size:94% position:6%
was your international
experience,

00:03:09.889 --> 00:03:12.358
did that make you ready for
an American high school,

00:03:12.358 --> 00:03:15.895 align:start size:94% position:6%
or not ready for
an American high school?

00:03:15.895 --> 00:03:17.463 align:start size:94% position:6%
-No, not --
I would say not ready.

00:03:17.463 --> 00:03:20.900
I mean I -- because most of the
schools I'd gone to were --

00:03:20.900 --> 00:03:23.503 align:start size:94% position:6%
they were like --
they were military schools.

00:03:23.503 --> 00:03:25.772 align:start size:94% position:6%
So other kids
were always coming in,

00:03:25.772 --> 00:03:27.006 line:92%
and everybody was, like, "Hey,"

00:03:27.006 --> 00:03:30.009
and welcoming each other,
but when I moved to Alabama

00:03:30.009 --> 00:03:31.644 size:88% position:44%
everybody had been there
and grown up together.

00:03:31.644 --> 00:03:34.681 align:start size:94% position:6%
So, you know,
I just felt like a real dork.

00:03:34.681 --> 00:03:37.584 align:start size:94% position:6%
You know, I was like,
"Hey, nice to meet everybody,"

00:03:37.584 --> 00:03:40.353 align:start size:94% position:6%
and everyone was, like,
"No, who are you?"

00:03:40.353 --> 00:03:41.621 size:88% position:44% line:92%
Like, "Get out of here."

00:03:41.621 --> 00:03:42.488 line:92%
-Did you at least like --

00:03:42.488 --> 00:03:45.391 align:start size:94% position:6%
Was it true you were in Korea
for a while?

00:03:45.391 --> 00:03:45.925 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
-Yeah, yeah.

00:03:45.925 --> 00:03:48.795 align:start size:94% position:6%
-So did you at least know what
American pop culture was

00:03:48.795 --> 00:03:49.429 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
or American style?

00:03:49.429 --> 00:03:53.700 align:start size:94% position:6%
-We had like one American
station on the TV,

00:03:53.700 --> 00:03:57.103 align:start size:94% position:6%
so I knew
"Jeopardy!" and cartoons.

00:03:57.103 --> 00:03:59.105 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
[ Laughter ]

00:03:59.105 --> 00:04:02.041
But no, I mean, my parents were,
first of all, they're not --

00:04:02.041 --> 00:04:03.543 align:start size:94% position:6%
I love them,
they're such wonderful,

00:04:03.543 --> 00:04:05.678 align:start size:94% position:6%
wonderful people,
but they weren't, like, hip.

00:04:05.678 --> 00:04:06.379 size:78% position:39% line:92%
You know what I mean?

00:04:06.379 --> 00:04:08.781 align:start size:94% position:6%
So they were like going --
And my mom's so cheap.

00:04:08.781 --> 00:04:13.686 align:start size:94% position:6%
So we would go to this Korean
market called Itaewon,

00:04:13.686 --> 00:04:14.821 line:92%
and she would buy us, like,

00:04:14.821 --> 00:04:18.725 align:start size:94% position:6%
the cheapest knockoff,
like, members only.

00:04:18.725 --> 00:04:21.461 align:start size:94% position:6%
The velcro sneakers,
so basically when I showed up

00:04:21.461 --> 00:04:22.262 size:78% position:39% line:92%
to school in Alabama,

00:04:22.262 --> 00:04:24.097
everyone had their whatever was
cool in Alabama,

00:04:24.097 --> 00:04:26.833 align:start size:94% position:6%
their polo shirts, and I had
like, a guy on the horse,

00:04:26.833 --> 00:04:27.767 align:start size:94% position:6%
But it wasn't.
-Right.

00:04:27.767 --> 00:04:29.135 align:start size:94% position:6%
-It wasn't the right guy.
[ Laughter ]

00:04:29.135 --> 00:04:31.871
He wasn't playing polo.
I don't know what he was doing.

00:04:31.871 --> 00:04:33.473 align:start size:94% position:6%
He was playing
a different sport.

00:04:33.473 --> 00:04:34.173 size:81% position:41% line:92%
-It was a weird horse.

00:04:34.173 --> 00:04:36.909
-It was a weird horse.
It didn't have four legs,

00:04:36.909 --> 00:04:37.644 size:84% position:42% line:92%
it had like three legs.

00:04:37.644 --> 00:04:39.646
'cause they -- you know,
'cause of copyright things.

00:04:39.646 --> 00:04:42.815
So, yeah, I was wearing clothes
from like a different decade.

00:04:42.815 --> 00:04:44.417 align:start size:94% position:6%
It was bad.
-That's fantastic.

00:04:44.417 --> 00:04:45.585 align:start size:94% position:6%
I'm glad everything worked out
for you,

00:04:45.585 --> 00:04:48.655
and you found a place where
you're comfortable and happy.

00:04:48.655 --> 00:04:49.722 align:start size:94% position:6%
The woods.
-In the woods.

00:04:49.722 --> 00:04:51.858 align:start size:94% position:6%
Where you can survive
in the woods.

00:04:51.858 --> 00:04:52.425 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
-That's right.

00:04:52.425 --> 00:04:53.326 line:92%
-Thanks so much for being here.

00:04:53.326 --> 00:04:55.695 align:start size:94% position:6%
I'm so excited for the show.
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:04:55.695 --> 00:04:57.897 align:start size:94% position:6%
And I am so happy
to be working with you.

00:04:57.897 --> 00:04:59.532 line:92%
Glenn Howerton, everybody.

